WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.025
Before you type anything into a chatbot, ask: what should I hand to AI at all?

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:12.250
Split the assignment. Support work: formatting references, checking grammar, organizing your notes.

3
00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:21.183
Core work: forming the argument, analyzing the data, reflecting on your experience. That is the skill the assignment is building.

4
00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:26.508
Delegate the core work, and the result may look good, but you skipped the learning.

5
00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:35.067
Three questions before you delegate. Is this the skill I am meant to build? Is AI allowed here, and how? Can I check the result?

6
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:41.458
Whatever you delegate, you keep the final decision. You are responsible for what you submit.

7
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:47.283
Try it now: mark each part of your next assignment keep, delegate, or get feedback.

8
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:53.342
Pen out. Support work can save time. Core work is where the learning is.

9
00:00:53.792 --> 00:00:58.817
If it is the skill being built, keep it, and use AI for feedback instead.

10
00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.267
And you are responsible for what you submit.
